rest). Defaults to ","type":"text"},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" if not specified.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"printsObject"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For most elements, any program will compute a default x and y position. The position attributes let this be changed two ways.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"position"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The font attribute group gathers together attributes for determining the font within a credit or direction. They are based on the text styles for Cascading Style Sheets. The font-family is a comma-separated list of font names.The font-style can be normal or italic. The font-size can be one of the CSS sizes or a numeric point size. The font-weight can be normal or bold. The default is application-dependent, but is a text font vs. a music font.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"font"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"color"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Indicates whether the alteration should appear to the left or the right of the preceding element.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"location"}]}],"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLHarmonyAlter":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLHarmonyAlter","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLHarmonyAlter","type":"topic","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLHarmonyAlter","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLHarmonyAlter","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The harmony-alter type represents the chromatic alteration of the root, numeral, or bass of the current"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"harmony-chord group within the harmony element. In some chord styles, the text of the preceding element may"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"include alteration information. In that case, the print-object attribute of this type can be set to no. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"location attribute indicates whether the alteration should appear to the left or the right of the preceding"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element. Its default value varies by element."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlharmonyalter"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPosition":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLPosition","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLPosition","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLPosition","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"For most elements, any program will compute a default x and y position. The position attributes let this be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"changed two ways."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlposition","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLLeftRight":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The left-right type is used to indicate whether one element appears to the left or the right of another"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"element."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLeftRight","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLLeftRight","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLLeftRight","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLLeftRight","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlleftright"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLFont":{"title":"MXLFont","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlfont","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLFont","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFont","abstract":[{"text":"The font attribute group gathers together attributes for determining the font within a credit or direction.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"They are based on the text styles for Cascading Style Sheets. The font-family is a comma-separated list of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"font names. The font-style can be normal or italic. The font-size can be one of the CSS sizes or a numeric"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"point size. The font-weight can be normal or bold. The default is application-dependent, but is a text font"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vs. a music font."}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLFont","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLHarmonyAlter/init(value:printsObject:position:font:color:location:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Creates a new ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MXLHarmonyAlter"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"title":"init(value:printsObject:position:font:color:location:)","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlharmonyalter\/init(value:printsobject:position:font:color:location:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"value","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"printsObject","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"position","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLPosition","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL11MXLPositionV"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"font","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLFont","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLFontV"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"color","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLColor","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"location","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLLeftRight","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLLeftRightO"},{"text":"?)","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLHarmonyAlter\/init(value:printsObject:position:font:color:location:)"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLColor":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcolor","title":"MXLColor","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The color type indicates the color of an element. Color may be represented as hexadecimal RGB triples, as in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"HTML, or as hexadecimal ARGB tuples, with the A indicating alpha of transparency. An alpha value of 00 is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"totally transparent; FF is totally opaque. If RGB is used, the A value is assumed to be FF."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor"}}}